# Every deploy may change contract addresses inside app.js, and a stale client points at a
# drained legacy game whose every action reverts. no-cache does NOT mean "don't cache" — it means
# revalidate before use, so unchanged files still ride the ETag to a 304 and only real deploys
# actually re-download. A user found this the hard way: an old cached app.js dealt against a
# migrated game and got "execution reverted" on every hand.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
